      "explanation": "Password authentication verifies a captured pre-reset hash and returns only userId. The route later calls establishSession(password), whose admission uses unconditional VALUES, unlike SIWE. A reset between these awaits revokes existing sessions but cannot revoke a not-yet-inserted one; the request authenticated with the old credential then creates a fresh, live password session. An email preclaimer knows that old password. The reset now marks email verified, so surviving session authority undermines recovery even though all wallet tombstones were correctly written.",
